# A silent ALSA default, so Wine's audio driver has something to open.
#
# This machine has /dev/snd but no PipeWire or PulseAudio session, so the usual
# `default` device cannot be opened, DirectSound fails at its first step, and
# every reconstructed audio function reads 0. ALSA's `null` plugin is built
# into libasound and needs no server: it accepts a stream and discards it.
#
#   ALSA_CONFIG_PATH=$PWD/tools/alsa/asoundrc
#
# Deliberately self-contained rather than including /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf.
# That file pre-loads /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf.d, where 99-pipewire-default
# points `default` at PipeWire through a hook that runs after anything this
# file says -- so an override here is simply lost, with "Host is down" as the
# only clue.
pcm.!default { type null }
ctl.!default { type null }
